{"id": "EUVD-2026-93327", "enisaUuid": "1b5a30f4-c886-385a-a87e-0dab6c38e96d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: wait for RCU readers before releasing dma_device\n\ndma_issue_pending_all() walks the dma_device_list with\nlist_for_each_entry_rcu() under rcu_read_lock(). dma_device_release()\nunlinks the device with list_del_rcu() and then calls\ndevice->device_release() (which in many drivers, such as plx_dma.c,\ndirectly calls kfree()).\n\nBecause there is no grace period between unlinking the device and\nfreeing it, concurrent RCU readers in dma_issue_pending_all() can\naccess the device after it has been freed.\n\nThe lockless walk originally relied on clients holding a dmaengine\nreference to pin the provider module, and therefore the device, for as\nlong as they might traverse the list. Commit 8ad342a86359 (\"dmaengine:\nAdd reference counting to dma_device struct\") decoupled the dma_device\nlifetime from the module reference, so the device can now be released\nwhile a reader is still walking the list.\n\nAdd synchronize_rcu() before the device is freed, so RCU readers are\nguaranteed to have finished. Keep it unconditional: providers that do\nnot implement device_release() free the device themselves once\ndma_async_device_unregister() returns. This call will delay for a grace\nperiod with dma_list_mutex held, which is safe and only teardown path is\ndelayed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac8ce9f89638d6d79875cca7d8ae42566a9bde15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14578c78405d51fa92e4ada4502a45f537c0fcb8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbb3310a5167e868a5e763e32b9a23b4d50669ee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8577a5ec4f7e00443015ef99f646def093121a1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4448a539a0c39141cccc67be6cacde0f35024313", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc1f4884f1d46fc7a8cee6e2997ecc9e8d1c7f77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aed7e47a10b94ea3c5171e8d1382081accd2e03", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc750422170a563c7a81f6e49d36bb02c62ae37f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98342", "GHSA-jvjw-jpr2-5gjp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05da5886-af31-3905-bad7-0d077fff2dc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "05e4390e-dac1-396d-a6d5-abc6d5c20f01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <cbb3310a5167e868a5e763e32b9a23b4d50669ee"}, {"id": "0ae1bab9-d63b-31c7-85a8-390f9bd7216d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <fc1f4884f1d46fc7a8cee6e2997ecc9e8d1c7f77"}, {"id": "2e0f15c1-c82e-3a88-b021-085f40b07911", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "68685090-7e76-3191-9a4f-ce65d0f03c72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <14578c78405d51fa92e4ada4502a45f537c0fcb8"}, {"id": "71a4bf99-acf1-3532-9481-99bf4bc77532", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.29"}, {"id": "74f21ee1-17f0-3a3f-bb0d-7c9b5d0c6f2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "7729ada3-d5ee-3142-83db-2a511c6e4715", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "777b6191-5f95-3d04-845b-1bc79bcef7f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "8349f31e-5c0a-3252-9cc6-42a8459b4411", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "98513ab2-95e5-305a-9a7c-cfa0989da7fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <4aed7e47a10b94ea3c5171e8d1382081accd2e03"}, {"id": "985679c1-e5b8-3096-ba00-418bec7d2f73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <dc750422170a563c7a81f6e49d36bb02c62ae37f"}, {"id": "b0c14808-ca3d-3568-8259-0faa743e9e0a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <8577a5ec4f7e00443015ef99f646def093121a1b"}, {"id": "b95ee159-6976-382b-8c0f-1850780520c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "b98a5cb8-7e76-32ac-bb1b-4b576b4afd04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <4448a539a0c39141cccc67be6cacde0f35024313"}, {"id": "c36d9063-f5cb-37df-b052-d139db5147de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "cf4af626-7208-3052-9a70-bfe2cfa4ebc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ba05622b8b143b0c95968ba59bddfbd6d2f2559 <ac8ce9f89638d6d79875cca7d8ae42566a9bde15"}, {"id": "e4f6c896-bdc6-39b7-ab14-e9783f9c1815", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1b3a50e2-348a-3566-a2e4-d93b477b55a6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}